ection of small bubbles formed by mixing an extinguishing agent with water, used to cover and extinguish fires.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["froth"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}]}, {"definition": "A material formed by trapping pockets of gas in a liquid or solid.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["A foam mat can soften a hard seat."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(figuratively, poetic) The sea.", "tags": ["countable", "figuratively", "poetic", "uncountable"], "examples": ["He is in Europe, across the foam."], "quotes": [{"text": "How slowly does sad Time his feathers moue? / Hast thee O fayrest Planet to thy home / Within the Westerne fome:", "reference": "1595, Edmund Spenser, Epithalamion:"}, {"text": "You must dwell beyond the foam, / But I am safe and live at home.", "reference": "1885, Robert Louis Stevenson, “Foreign Children”, in A Child’s Garden of Verses, London: Longmans, Green, page 34:"}, {"text": "But as for me, I'd sooner be\nA-roaring here at home\nAbout the rolling, roaring life\nOf them that sails the foam.", "reference": "1918, Norman Lindsay, The Magic Pudding, Sydney: Angus and Robertson, page 171:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Fury, rage, ire.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(African-American Vernacular, in the plural) Sneakers.", "tags": ["countable", "in plural", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/foʊm/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/fəʊm/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}], "forms": [{"word": "foams", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "foaming", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "foamed", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "foamed", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(intransitive) To form or emit foam.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[…] And that is it\nHath made me rig my navy; at whose burthen\nThe anger'd ocean foams; with which I meant\nTo scourge the ingratitude that despiteful Rome\nCast on my noble father.", "reference": "c. 1606–1607 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Tragedie of Anthonie and Cleopatra”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act II, scene vi]:"}, {"text": "When the fierce North-wind with his airy forces\nRears up the Baltic to a foaming fury;", "reference": "1706, Isaac Watts, The Day of Judgement, lines 1–2:"}, {"text": "They were both silent for a measure of moments, and then Syme's speech came with a rush, like the sudden foaming of champagne.", "reference": "1908, G[ilbert] K[eith] Chesterton, chapter 8, in The Man Who Was Thursday: A Nightmare, Bristol: J[ames] W[illiams] Arrowsmith, […]; London: Simpkin, Marshall, Hamilton, Kent & Company, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "пеня се"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "escumar"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "schuimen"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "ŝaŭmi"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "vaahdota"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "écumer"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "mousser"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "schäumen"}, {"language": {"code": "got", "name": "Gothic"}, "word": "𐍈𐌰𐌸𐌾𐌰𐌽"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αφρίζω"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "habzik"}, {"language": {"code": "io", "name": "Ido"}, "word": "spumifar"}, {"language": {"code": "izh", "name": "Ingrian"}, "word": "koohuissa"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "発泡する"}, {"language": {"code": "la", "name": "Latin"}, "word": "spūmō"}, {"language": {"code": "lv", "name": "Latvian"}, "word": "putot"}, {"language": {"code": "ml", "name": "Malayalam"}, "word": "പതയുക"}, {"language": {"code": "mi", "name": "Māori"}, "word": "whakahuka"}, {"language": {"code": "mr", "name": "Marathi"}, "word": "फेसाळणे"}, {"language": {"code": "enm", "name": "Middle English"}, "word": "fomen"}, {"language": {"code": "enm", "name": "Middle English"}, "word": "femen"}, {"language": {"code": "ang", "name": "Old English"}, "word": "fǣman"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "pienić się"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "espumar"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "spumega"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "spuma"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "пе́ниться"}, {"language": {"code": "sh", "name": "Serbo-Croatian"}, "word": "пе̏нити"}, {"language": {"code": "sh", "name": "Serbo-Croatian"}, "word": "pȅniti"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "espumar"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "espumear"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "skumma"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "köpürmek"}, {"language": {"code": "ota", "name": "Ottoman Turkish"}, "word": "كوپورمك"}, {"language": {"code": "cy", "name": "Welsh"}, "word": "ewynnu"}, {"language": {"code": "yi", "name": "Yiddish"}, "word": "שוימען"}, {"language": {"code": "yi", "name": "Yiddish"}, "word": "פּינען"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To spew saliva as foam; to foam at the mouth.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[…] to London will we march amain,\nAnd once again bestride our foaming steeds,\nAnd once again cry ‘Charge upon our foes!’\nBut never once again turn back and fly.", "reference": "c. 1591–1592 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Third Part of Henry the Sixt, […]”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act II, scene i]:"}, {"text": "Master, I have brought unto thee my son, which hath a dumb spirit; And wheresoever he taketh him, he teareth him: and he foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth away.", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Mark 9:17-18:"}, {"text": "But I was talking to the wind; for whether my tears, my attitude, or the disorder of my dress prov'd fresh incentives, or whether he was not under the dominion of desires he could not bridle, but snorting and foaming with lust and rage, he renews his attack, seizes me, and again attempts to extend and fix me on the settee […]", "reference": "1749, [John Cleland], “[Letter the First]”, in Memoirs of a Woman of Pleasure [Fanny Hill], volume I, London: […] [Thomas Parker] for G. Fenton [i.e., Fenton and Ralph Griffiths] […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(firefighting) To coat or cover with foam.", "tags": [], "examples": ["It used to be common practice to foam the runway prior to an emergency landing, in case a fuel-fed fire occurred."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foam", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}